  "report": "Initial stage, retained from the supplied prior findings: A04 and A05 explicitly narrate Experiment acquisition, covering five product-action categories: four for A04 and one for A05. A01 reports cart re-addition only. A02 concerns Dr. Idriss; A12’s purchases concern Regimen Lab. All other requested initial focal counts were zero. Earlier exact records were not re-retrieved; their findings and contextual evidence below rely on the supplied prior findings.\n\nUpdated stage: Three focal accounts explicitly narrate Experiment acquisition (A04, A05, A11), totaling six product-action assertions. A11 adds one Softwear stock-up category, not three assertions for three unopened tubes. A14 adds gifted Buffer Jelly receipt; A15 adds contemplated Plasma Wash return; A16 adds intended Continuum substitution for existing azelaic-acid and salicylic-acid products. No completed return or explicit completed routine replacement is reported. Verified-buyer metadata for A15/A16 does not establish narrated acquisition.\n\nBuying reasons remain bounded: A04 describes sister introduction, favorable experience, nighttime hydration/repair goals and launch-time expansion; A05 describes instant Avant Guard checkout after TikTok discovery amid sustainability concerns. A11 explicitly stocked up while loving Softwear, then reported dermatitis, prescribed steroid cream, recovery and a worse flare within 24 hours of retrying. This supports the actor’s adverse-reaction attribution, not medically confirmed causation. Influencer recommendation is discovery context, not an explicit isolated stock-up motive. Their loss of usable stock and stated $70 CAD loss coexist with affection, envy of successful users and qualified encouragement to try it. Remedy acquisition is not Experiment acquisition.\n\nThe three credited retailer-review origins repeat completed Experiment acquisition at brand level, but not one identical product-specific checkout motivation. A04 and A11 share favorable experience preceding further acquisition across different products. For the precise proposition that liking Softwear prompted stock-up, A11 and context-only cowrunamuck provide distinct-actor reported reasons across retailer-review and community roles; cowrunamuck additionally cites formerly difficult direct-shipping access. This contextual corroboration does not increase focal counts or establish general buying causation.\n\nMaterial context, outside focal counts: cowrunamuck (Reddit, September 5, 2025; score 21) reports two Softwear backups, smoothness, moisture, sensitive-skin compatibility, no scent, preference over Eadem and approval of Sephora availability. RowanVC (same thread/date; score 42) praises Softwear/Experiment, but an unspecified balm stash does not establish Experiment stockpiling; their Dr. Idriss testimony concerns tackiness and layering, often with lanolin, followed by soft lips. These are separate contextual actors, not testimony donated to A01/A02. Their favorable Softwear experience and A11’s later intolerance make tolerability evidence mixed. Contextual opening-post identities/engagement are unavailable; product pages and metadata resolve scope without adding customer origins.\n\nOther experience evidence is conditional and mixed. A14’s favorable Buffer Jelly report follows only two uses mixed into nighttime moisturizer with rosacea; it supports a positive nighttime skin experience alongside A04, not isolated product efficacy or paid conversion. A15’s detailed unsuccessful cleansing trials and severe eye burning oppose A04’s favorable face-wash account, although A04’s exact cleanser SKU is unconfirmed. A15’s suspected defect or misuse remains unresolved. A16 reports reduced overnight acne redness and no sensitivity while explicitly declining to judge acne/pigmentation efficacy; intended simplification is not completed replacement. A05’s imperfect mask fit coexists with approval and joint use of hydrating products. A02’s aversion and A12’s size complaint remain other-brand evidence.\n\nRaw engagement: A01 score 13, A02 score 4, A12 score 12; prior findings classify these as not materially positive/not interpreted. A04, A05, A11, A14, A15 and A16 each have 0 upvotes and 0 downvotes. All engagement observation times are unavailable. Context scores 21 and 42 are retained separately, without enough exposure context to award material resonance. No resonance posture is awarded. Likes/scores establish neither verified experience, independence, prevalence nor buying effects. Review update timestamps add neither origins nor events. Formula versions remain unknown; detailed testimony is distinguished from generic approval, and no broad repurchase, remedy-driven Experiment purchasing or market-causal conclusion follows.",
